  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malala Fund for Girls&apos; Right to Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Established in 2012, the Malala Fund for Girls&#x2019; Right to Education expands access to quality education for girls and women, particularly those affected by conflict, disaster, and exclusion. Its interventions increase access to learning opportunities, improve education quality through gender-transformative teaching and learning environments, and strengthen policies and institutional capacity for sustainable change. Supported by multiple donors, the Fund promotes system-wide improvements across formal, non-formal, and informal education. It addresses harmful gender norms and stereotypes that hinder learning and skills development while advancing girls&#x2019; and women&#x2019;s empowerment</narrative>
  </description>
